cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use cleanCT in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "cleanCT: Non-destructive metal-base removal and inspection of micro-CT wood scans"
abstract: >-
  cleanCT is a native Windows application (PySide6 / Qt 6) for micro-CT scans of wood
  specimens mounted on a metal base. It locates the metal base and the wood, shows four
  guide lines for review, removes the base with a metal-removal engine, and exports the
  inner wood region as DICOM and NIfTI with a verified bundle.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-19
authors:
  - family-names: Hartanto
    given-names: Benedictus Reynaldo
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/benedictusrey/cleanCT"
url: "https://github.com/benedictusrey/cleanCT"
keywords:
  - micro-CT
  - wood
  - metal artefact removal
  - DICOM
  - NIfTI
  - volumetric analysis
  - non-destructive testing
